<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38782" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπευφημ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>assent with a shout of applause,</i> c.
			inf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάντες ἐπευφήμησαν Ἀχαιοὶ αἰδεῖσθαί
					θ᾽ ἱερῆα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.22
				</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.295
			</span></i>: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Galb.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.
			pers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἥρην ἐ.</span>
			<i>glorify, sing praises to</i> her, <i><span class="en">
				Musae.
				275
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc. et
			dat. rei, <i>sing over</i> or <i>in furtherance of,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοαῖσι . . ὕμνους ἐπευφημεῖτε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					620
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπευφήμησαν εὐχαῖσιν . . παιᾶνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IT</u>
					1403
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> c. dupl. acc.,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμὰς τύχας παιᾶν᾽ ἐπηυφήμησεν</span>
			<i>sang</i> a paean <i>over</i> my fortunes, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				350.4
			</span></i>; folld. by dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. παιᾶνα τἠμῇ
				συμφορᾷ Ἄρτεμιν</span>
			<i>sing</i> the paean <i>in praise of</i> her over my fate,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IA</u>
				1467
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> c. acc. et
			dat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. νόστον τινί</span>
			<i>wish</i> them <i>a happy</i> return, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.556
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b> c. dupl.
			acc., <i>call for the sake of good omen,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				<u>All.</u>
				68
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν παῖδες οἱ ἥρωες -οῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					3p.425M.
				</span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
